Pipe shells' mitred corners where the intersection of the two sides
breaks up (mitcad#1559). Applies after 1661.

BRepFill_TrimShellCorner trims a corner's two sides against each other
along their intersection. Two sides of one section touch where their
normals coincide (on the corner's sides), and at a small corner they meet
at a shallow angle all round: there the intersection of approximated sides
comes in pieces with gaps of 1e-4 to 0.1 mm and loops of its own, the trim
finds no loop round the section, and the caller carried the section
unturned through the corner, leaning by the corner's angle.

When that trim fails for a mitred corner (BRepFill_Right) of a closed
section, each side is now cut where it crosses the bisector plane, which
both cross well apart from each other (at more than a right angle less
half the corner's). The two cuts are one where the pieces are straight
near the corner (the sides are then the prisms of their end sections,
1664) and lie within the bend over the mitre's depth of each other
elsewhere. The loop round the section is broken where the U-edges of
either side cross the plane (into one vertex where the two sides' meet);
each edge between two breaks lies on one face of each side, runs through
the middles of the two cuts, and has each side's cut as its curve on that
side's face. Each side's U-edges end at the breaks, and each face's bound
is replaced by its edges, as the trim along the intersection makes them.
The mitre is refused where the two cuts lie further apart than 5e-4 of
the section's extent (the corners of about 60 degrees of curved pieces,
0.011 mm apart on an 8 mm circle, which the trim along the intersection
of a two-edged section makes instead).

ChooseSection asked BRepExtrema_ExtCC for the points of the extremum of
two edges that are parallel, which have a distance but no points, and
crashed; it now takes them as edges without an extremum.

An 8 mm pipe along the intersection curve of a sine wave drawn as ten
lines on XZ and an arc on XY, and along two B-spline pieces meeting at 3,
0.3 and 0.05 degrees, is now mitred, square to the path within 0.0002
degrees, its volume within 0.0004 %; it leaned up to 78.7 degrees and
held 32.6 % less (the ten lines), 3, 0.3 and 0.05 degrees.

